WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.660
When the rest of us had been caught,
we only had one last hope--

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.290
Kosame! I knew you were strong!

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.950
Hototo gets revenge! The race goes on!

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.950
But we still don't know
the true identity of Gil.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:49.450
As a result of talks within B.I.G. BOSS,
they've decided the race will go on.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.790
Thanks to Kosame.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.330
No, no! I hardly did anything!

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:55.410
Sounds like you guys had fun.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:02:00.080
I got stuck with this joke of a man
and almost died of boredom.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.450
Hmph. Your face is a joke.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.160
I don't wanna hear it from you, pal.
Not with that shabby hair.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.500
Sh-Shabby?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.330
Ahem! Unfortunately,
the threat of Gil still remains.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.700
It's possible he'll ambush the route again.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.700
As such, we want to shift
the next supply point up to this city,

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.040
which will take the race
on this northern route.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.830
It's quite the detour.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.330
For the safety of the staff involved,
we had to pick a city on the railway.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.870
We would've preferred
a faster path through the plains

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.950
to show off the superiority of cars, but...

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.040
It beats the race getting canceled altogether.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.160
Agreed! Safety first!

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.200
Me, too.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.370
Whatever.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.540
Screw that. Let's do the exciting route.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.410
Quit if you don't like it. We'll celebrate.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.250
Eh?!

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:59.160
Um, your employer, Iron Motor Company,
has already approved it, so...

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.830
Tsk!

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:03.500
Mr. Reaseman?

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.120
I think this race is a bit too dangerous for me.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.160
I'd like to retire.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.120
Huh? Uh...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.410
Right...

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.500
Richard.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.540
You witnessed what happened firsthand,
so I can't blame you.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.330
Don't stress over it.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.540
Now then, you'll need to stay here
while we change supply points.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:34.200
Tomorrow morning, you'll go there
together and the race will resume.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.540
You hear that, Appare? We get the whole day off!

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.160
"Episode 9: short break"
You hear that, Appare? We get the whole day off!

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.790
"Episode 9: short break"
Gee, Kosame. You're so helpful.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:44.040
Thanks to you, we always get
to eat such yummy food and--

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:44.950
What are you doing?

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:50.700
Uh! It's Appare's fault! He never
hears a thing while he's working!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.250
--Does it run hotter than I thought?
--What's he fixing?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.250
--Does it run hotter than I thought?
--The cooling for
the hybrid engine or something.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.830
--Or maybe my calculations for cooling are off.
--The cooling for
the hybrid engine or something.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.830
If I can just improve efficiency by 20%--

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:03.450
If you need help,
you could always ask Mr. Carter.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:04.790
Who's that?

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.000
He heard <i>you</i>.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.830
Seth from GM. You know, fancy glasses.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:10.660
Oh...

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.700
He was originally a GM engineer.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.830
Maybe he'll give you an idea or two.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.450
Come again!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.330
Mr. Aldin.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.410
Call me Dylan. I'm not a fan of formalities.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.910
Dylan... I finally avenged my father.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.370
Seems that way.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.450
It's because of all the things you told me.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:44.910
On his name and mine, I won't forget this debt.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.370
Don't burden yourself. Live freely.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:51.370
Thank you.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:57.370
Good grief. If kids are thanking me,
I'm doomed as an outlaw.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.870
Who's Claudia?

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.790
Hey, you okay?

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.370
Where'd you hear that?

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:08.000
You were staring at a photo
at the pre-race party.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.830
Claudia...

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:16.160
I'm sorry. You looked sad, so...

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.330
Claudia was...

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:26.580
...someone who laughed like a child,
even in a world as filthy as this.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.540
Was?

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:33.700
All I wanted... was to protect her, and yet...

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.700
If there's someone you
wanna protect, keep 'em close.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.000
Someone I wanna protect?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.370
If not, even better.
You might be happier that way.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.250
How much can this thing cool?

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.160
Huh? Um, well...

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:59.540
It's driven over 900 miles.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.870
By morning, I want every
nut and bolt double-checked.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.950
But, unless the mechanics get rest...

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.620
If anyone wants to rest, let 'em. They're fired.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:14.580
Got it? Listen up!
My-- GM's future depends on it!

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:19.120
We must win this race at all costs!
We deserve to win!

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:23.040
Against Iron! Against BNW!
Against the bumpkin monkeys--

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.290
Then service it yourself.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.040
Gah! What are you doing here?!

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.040
Inspecting.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.080
Well, don't!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.700
Are you Seth?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.040
How cheeky for a monkey.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.910
Call me Mr. Carter.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.200
You an engineer?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:42.160
No! As GM's representative,
I'm one of the people in charge of this race.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.700
I see. Then you're useless to me.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.910
What did you come here for?

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:49.700
For ideas.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:55.620
To improve my hybrid engine's
parallel heat exchange cooling system.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:59.700
Huh? Hybrid? Heat exchange? What?

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.040
Heat from the gas engine
drives the steam engine

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.540
to increase thermal efficiency
and boost power while--

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.540
No point explaining if you're not an engineer.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:15.580
No way... You're using the power
of two engines in parallel?

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:16.620
You understand?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:22.500
No... Such a thing isn't possible!
And if it was, you couldn't make it!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.540
Wanna see it?

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:24.950
I'll pass.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.910
All right.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.950
--That's a good machine.
--Huh?

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:33.200
Not sure about the weird empty spot
by the engine though.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.950
It's almost complete!

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:39.950
If we use this to compress air
and improve combustion,

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:42.160
for a short while, it'll boost power and--

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.830
What'll it cost?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:48.910
Just do your job. You've spent enough
time and money on that weird device.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.080
But this would--

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:53.540
If you can't follow our policies, you're canned.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:58.870
I'm expecting a lot from you.
Don't disappoint me.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.330
What could you possibly know?

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:11.540
I'll never go back to being a filthy engineer!

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.580
They all look so good.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.000
Hurry up and decide, Sarge.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.500
Gimme this much in apple pies.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.290
R-Right!

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.660
Nice flaky crust, warm gooey apples,

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.750
the smell of cinnamon tickling your nose...

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.040
It's finger-lickin' good!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.750
Why did you make me wear the mask?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.000
Was there a line?

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.790
You're such a clever guy, Bro!

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:57.910
I said don't call me that.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.080
Huh?

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.910
Wanna piece of pie?

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.500
Thanks.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.040
What's up? That's a pretty sad face for a child.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.080
Shut up. I'm not a child.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.870
That's what all children say.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.580
Do you have someone you wanna protect?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.160
Huh? That came outta nowhere.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.290
Can't say I do.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:38.250
It's on you to protect yourself.
That's the code of us outlaws.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:39.700
I see.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.950
What will you do after the race?

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:47.540
If I won money, I think I'd
buy some land and retire, but...

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:51.870
Not sure if that fits my style. How about you?

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.950
I'll protect my family.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.750
Yeah? Pretty noble for a kid.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.160
Let me tell you one thing--

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.500
What you wanna protect and
what you should aren't always the same.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:10.290
Think real hard about what you protect.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:15.870
Also, you can't protect anyone
if you can't protect yourself. Get strong first.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.290
Also, brush your teeth after snacks.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.700
If I need to keep the hybrid engine
at optimal temperature...

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:32.120
How do I step up the cooling?
Expand the cooling system?

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.660
But there's not enough space in the engine room.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:39.040
--Is increasing air circulation the only option?
--Watch where you're going, idiot!

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:39.870
--Make it shine real good.
These shoes are worth--

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:42.290
--If I attach ducts to the Appare
to use as intake...
--Make it shine real good.
These shoes are worth--

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.330
--If I attach ducts to the Appare
to use as intake...

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:49.450
Hey, hey, hey! You guys are cheaping out on me!

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:57.500
What's the matter?! I'm right here!
Nobody's gonna claim the bounty?!

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:05.660
What a boring town.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.750
That's the price of the mighty.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.660
Eh?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.040
That loneliness.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.450
I ain't lonely, I'm bored!

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:16.330
Don't be ashamed to be lonely.
It's proof of the powerful.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.580
I ain't ashamed, 'cuz I ain't lonely!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:19.660
Hello.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:23.660
Lonely or bored? Let's settle it with a match.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.580
You're on.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.700
Huh? What, really?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.250
A drinking contest.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.330
That's fine by me.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:33.620
Al!

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:36.660
Just one shot of tequila?

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.450
And you thought you stood a chance? You're nuts!

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.330
You okay?

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.950
Take the baby home and get lost.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:52.040
Huh? Or do you wanna take me on instead?

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.870
Very well.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.000
Huh? Done already?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.910
Let's do another shot!

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.540
We're just getting started!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.830
Sofia... Can we go...?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.700
Already? Hmph! If you insist...

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:21.950
Thank you, everyone! Good day!

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.290
That lady can drink!

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:30.450
Sofia... She's a keeper...

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:47.160
Man, what a privilege it is
to cut the famous Dylan's hair!

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:52.000
You're one of the Hundred Four?
Woo! The big four!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:56.660
Wait, was it five? The Hundred... Oh, Nine!

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:58.000
It's "Thousand Three."

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.120
Oh! Thousand Three!

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.790
I prefer not to be called--

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:07.830
My, you're so modest!
Oh! Think you can shoot a hole in the wall?

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:12.620
You could sign it and everything!
It'd be great for business and my customers--

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.330
Just shut up and cut!

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:16.450
Oh my.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.910
--The problem is the emergency booster.
--Welcome!

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.750
How to hold back the heat at normal speed?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.040
Have a seat.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:28.830
--Going at high speed
gives a greater benefit, but...
--Hmm. Shall I cut it short for you?

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:29.660
Short?

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.410
Just a moment.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.370
That's it! I could cut the plumbing shorter.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.200
If the coolant takes
a shorter route and runs parallel...

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.200
Impressive. I was really trying to hit you.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:27.160
Well, against an ordinary opponent,
I wouldn't have to draw it.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:30.410
Kosame, do you hate using a katana?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.790
Huh?

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:35.540
Because of what happened
to your mother, I could see why.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:39.040
And yet, you became this strong with it?

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:43.080
It's more fear and respect than hate.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.950
That's why I became strong--

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:49.750
so I wouldn't get hurt or have to hurt anyone.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.580
Who did you learn kung fu from?

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.870
My father. "Life isn't easy."

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.910
Especially for women!

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.790
Get stronger!

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:09.290
More! Even more!

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.250
Sounds like he was strict.

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.580
Yeah. When I said I was entering this race...

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.000
Only if you defeat me!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.750
I'll break your arm to stop you if I must!

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.250
My goodness... And?

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.540
I beat him.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.910
My father's really old fashioned.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.540
I get it, though.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:35.910
He's afraid to let his cute daughter
join such a dangerous race.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.000
Cute?

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:43.330
Wha--?! No! I have a little sister,
so I can understand why he'd worry!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.160
I see.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.910
Hey, Kosame!

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:51.290
We're going soon. Get ready.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:55.790
Ooh, I can't wait! Oh, yeah!
Do you want to come with us?

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:58.160
Uh, sure...

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:01.000
Where do I put the supplementary cooling?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:05.790
On the side of the car?
That would be cooled by outside air

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:08.700
and dump heat away from the engine room.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.660
The risk would be... collisions.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:16.000
Considering the race thus far,
I have to factor in damage.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.620
But if I split the risk with one on each side...

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:23.660
So this is it? A real American hot spring!

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:25.500
There's a lot around here.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.580
It's been so long!

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.580
By the way, where's Appare?

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:33.580
I'm sure he's got his hands full
remodeling the car.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:36.450
I knew it! That might just work!

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:39.290
Hey, Kosame! I'm hungr--

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:40.500
Huh?

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:48.410
Wh-Who the heck are you?!

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:55.120
Engineers are 1% brilliant ideas
and 99% drive to bring them to life.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.200
Are you all right, Thomas?!

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.450
Yeah...

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.750
Sofia!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.750
Oh, Xialian! You came, too?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.500
Kosame invited me.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:11.200
Yeah? On a date?

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:12.080
Huh?

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.330
Am I interfering?

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:16.450
N-Not at all! Hototo came, too.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:21.160
I see. I guess it'll be
pretty lively with everyone here.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:27.540
Ooh, how fancy! That's America
for you--everything's big!

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.000
Hey. You guys came... too...?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.370
I didn't know Al was here!

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:33.750
--Squeak?
--Guess what? I tried tequila!

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.450
--Guess what? I tried tequila!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.290
Yeah? And how was... it...?

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.540
Huh?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.540
Why are you naked?!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:46.870
Why are you here?!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:48.040
Huh?

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:52.330
Kosame! Appare! What's wrong with you?!

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:53.330
Hmm?

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:54.700
What the...?

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:57.620
--That was a shock.
--What a coincidence!

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:58.500
--Yeah.
--What a coincidence!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:01.580
--There's only so much to do in the city, so...
--And here I came to relax. Go figure.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.370
--And here I came to relax. Go figure.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:09.330
Even though I had no idea, I'm very sorry.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.580
Cultures can be so different.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.830
Teach me some Japanese games.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.750
All right!

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:17.000
Cut your hair?

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:20.000
You wish. Of course not.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.450
Then why is your nape so clean?

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.410
It always was. Leave me alone.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.250
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:28.870
Look that way, hey!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:32.250
That's it! If you look
the way they point, you lose.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.580
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:34.910
Look that way, hey!

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:36.200
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.080
Look that way, hey!

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.250
Whoops! My bad!

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.580
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:44.120
--Grow up.
--Look that way, hey!

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:47.250
Oops! Sorry about that!

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:48.580
--Let me try.
--Huh?

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:50.040
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.790
Look that way, hey!

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:58.000
Oh? So I can point through your skull? Game on.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.250
You're dead.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.200
Um, it's not that sort of game...

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.660
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.290
Look that way, hey!

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.330
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:09.910
This is paradise.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.580
I'm getting dizzy.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.250
Well? Do you think you can win?

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.700
I want to, but it all comes down to luck.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:20.290
I hope you do.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:22.250
Aren't you cheering for Al?

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.910
More or less. But to be honest,

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:29.250
I want him to finish safely more than win.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:33.750
Yeah? Are you and Al lovers?

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:37.750
Not quite. If I had to say, we're like siblings.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:38.700
Siblings?

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:42.700
My mother worked at the Lyon Estate
as a live-in wet nurse.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:47.000
So Al and I grew up together just like siblings.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.120
Yeah?

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:51.870
When my mother wasn't able to work anymore,

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:57.200
Al's father asked me to be
Al's chaperon when I was just 14

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:00.540
so we could keep up the same lifestyle.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:04.540
And all this time I thought you lived in luxury.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.620
Not exactly.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:11.410
Do it again! Again!

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.160
Ready?!

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:15.700
Up you go!

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:19.330
Whew! Do that to me!

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:22.200
Look that way, punch!

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.870
Look that way, kick!

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.790
--<i>Gochandesu! Gochandesu!</i>
--You damn cheater!

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.660
<i>Nokotta! Nokotta!</i>

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.540
<i>Tsuppari! Tsuppari! Tsuppari!</i>

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:37.370
Hey! Enough horsing around!

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:40.200
Calm your asses down!

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:44.120
Hey, Appare! Where are you going?

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.830
It's time to get to work...

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:49.160
...on the finishing touches!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.200
Here. I made you a snack.

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:00.200
So salty.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:01.290
Huh?

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:04.660
Saltier than usual.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.500
You actually care how it tastes?

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.120
Of course I do.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:14.040
When people get tired,
don't they crave salty stuff?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.580
I see.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.200
You finished it, huh?

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:29.290
The hybrid engine's complete at last!

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:33.290
Yeah. The real race starts now.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:36.200
How far can we go?

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:39.120
Yeah! We can win this, Hototo!

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:41.120
--Squeak!
--Oh my!

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.120
The race is about to resume!

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:45.620
"North Platte, Nebraska"
The front row is Thousand Three's
Dylan the Hero and Crazy TJ!

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:47.660
The front row is Thousand Three's
Dylan the Hero and Crazy TJ!

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:54.200
Next is the crimson Jing Xialian, scion Al Lyon,
and the bizarre Team Appare!

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.830
In last, the fearsome Bad Brothers!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:00.790
All cars are standing by and ready to start!

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:06.700
You're Sofia, right?

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:08.290
Oh, Richard!

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:11.750
I'm off to New York, too.
Shall we ride together?

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:13.790
Sure, of course!

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:15.160
Shall I carry that?

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:17.500
No, I'm used to it!

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.450
"Next time"

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.910
"Episode 10: The Bridge To Hell"
